      "page_title": "Control Plane Components",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q1. What are the components of the Kubernetes control plane and what does each one do?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "The control plane is the cluster's brain: stores state, schedules, reconciles.",
            "==kube-apiserver== is the only front door",
            "==etcd== stores all cluster state",
            "Scheduler and controllers act on that state"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Component",
            "Job"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "kube-apiserver",
              "Auth, validate, REST"
            ],
            [
              "etcd",
              "Key-value state store"
            ],
            [
              "kube-scheduler",
              "Picks Pod's node"
            ],
            [
              "controller-manager",
              "Actual → desired"
            ],
            [
              "cloud-controller",
              "Cloud LBs, nodes, disks"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q2. What happens, step by step, when you run kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "The API server stores the manifest and controllers turn it into running containers.",
            "API server authenticates, validates, writes etcd",
            "Controllers make ReplicaSet, Pods; scheduler binds",
            "kubelet starts the containers"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml",
            "kubectl get pods -w",
            "# Pending → ContainerCreating",
            "# → Running"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "kubectl",
                "sub": "sends YAML",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "API server",
                "sub": "auth + validate",
                "ink": "red"
              },
              {
                "text": "etcd",
                "sub": "stores object",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "Controllers",
                "sub": "make Pods",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "Scheduler",
                "sub": "picks node",
                "ink": "orange"
              },
              {
                "text": "kubelet",
                "sub": "runs it",
                "ink": "pink"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q3. What is etcd and why does its health matter so much?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "etcd is a consistent key-value store holding every cluster object.",
            "==Raft== consensus needs quorum (2 of 3)",
            "Lost or corrupt: cluster state is gone",
            "Slow disks slow the whole API server"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "etcdctl endpoint health",
            "etcdctl snapshot save backup.db"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q4. What is the difference between control plane components and worker node components?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "The control plane decides what runs; workers run the Pods.",
            "Control plane: API server, etcd, scheduler, controllers",
            "Worker: ==kubelet==, kube-proxy, container runtime",
            "Running Pods survive a control plane outage"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "hero": "server",
      "aside": "etcd = memory!",
      "subtitle": "How the cluster thinks"
    },
