    {
      "page_title": "Pods",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q5. What is a Pod and why is it the smallest deployable unit instead of a container?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "A ==Pod== wraps containers that must run together on one node, so Kubernetes schedules the Pod, never a bare container.",
            "Share one **network** namespace, IP and volumes",
            "Scheduled, scaled, replaced as one unit"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "kind: Pod",
            "spec:",
            "  containers: [{name: app}]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q6. What is the difference between init containers and sidecar containers?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "==Init containers== run once to completion before the app starts; a ==sidecar== keeps running beside it.",
            "Init runs **in order**, each must succeed",
            "Sidecars: logging, proxies, sync",
            "Native sidecar: init + `restartPolicy: Always`"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "initContainers:",
            "- name: wait-db      # exits",
            "- name: log-agent",
            "  restartPolicy: Always # sidecar"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Pattern",
            "Role"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Init",
              "Setup, then exits"
            ],
            [
              "Sidecar",
              "Helper beside the app"
            ],
            [
              "Ambassador",
              "Proxy to outside services"
            ],
            [
              "Adapter",
              "Reshapes output, metrics"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q7. What are the Pod lifecycle phases and how do they differ from container states?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "A Pod ==phase== summarizes the whole Pod; ==container state== is per container.",
            "`CrashLoopBackOff` is a **Waiting** reason, not a phase"
          ]
        },
