        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q18. Are Kubernetes Secrets actually secure?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Not by default: only ==base64-encoded==, unencrypted in etcd.",
            "Anyone with get access reads them",
            "Anyone who can create a Pod mounts them",
            "Fix: encryption at rest, tight RBAC"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "# only base64, not secret",
            "echo cGFzczEyMw== | base64 -d",
            "# -> pass123"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q19. Env vars vs mounted files: what happens on update?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Env vars are read once; mounted volumes are kubelet-synced.",
            "Env vars change only on Pod restart",
            "Mounted files refresh in ~1 minute",
            "subPath mounts never update"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Method",
            "Live update?",
            "Best for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "envFrom / env",
              "{red:No}",
              "flags"
            ],
            [
              "Volume mount",
              "{green:Yes}, ~1 min",
              "config files"
            ],
            [
              "subPath mount",
              "{red:No}",
              "one file"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "none"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q20. How do you manage secrets safely in production?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Encrypt at rest and sync from a trusted store, never plaintext.",
            "==Encryption at rest==: KMS protects etcd",
            "==Sealed Secrets==: encrypted manifests in Git",
            "==External Secrets==: sync from Vault or cloud"
          ]
        },
