    {
      "page_title": "Troubleshooting Scenarios",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q37. A Pod is stuck in CrashLoopBackOff. How do you debug it?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "It keeps exiting, so find ==why it died== before restarting.",
            "`kubectl logs --previous` shows the crashed run",
            "`describe pod` shows exit code or **OOMKilled**",
            "Suspect bad config, missing Secret, failing probe"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "kubectl logs web-7d --previous",
            "kubectl describe pod web-7d",
            "# Last State: Terminated (137)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q38. A Pod is stuck in Pending. What do you check?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Pending means accepted, but the ==scheduler== found no node.",
            "Events show **FailedScheduling**",
            "Low CPU or memory, taints, affinity mismatch",
            "Unbound PVC also keeps it Pending"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "kubectl describe pod web-7d",
            "# 0/3 nodes: Insufficient cpu",
            "kubectl get pvc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q39. A Service is not reachable from other Pods. How do you troubleshoot it?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Walk outward: Service, selector, ==Endpoints==, then the Pod.",
            "Empty Endpoints: selector misses Pod labels",
            "`targetPort` must match the container's port",
            "Test DNS from a debug Pod"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "kubectl get endpoints web",
            "kubectl get pods --show-labels",
            "kubectl exec t -- nslookup web"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q40. A worker node goes NotReady. What happens to its Pods and what do you do?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Node marked unreachable, then ==evicts== Pods after a grace period.",
            "Unreachable taint evicts after **300s** default",
            "Deployments recreate Pods on healthy nodes",
            "Check kubelet, node conditions, disk pressure"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "kubectl describe node worker-2",
            "systemctl status kubelet",
            "journalctl -u kubelet -n 50"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "get pods",
                "sub": "read STATUS",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "describe",
                "sub": "read Events",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "logs",
                "sub": "--previous",
                "ink": "orange"
              },
              {
                "text": "fix cause",
                "sub": "then verify",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "banner",
          "title": "Key takeaways",
          "text": "Status shows where, Events show why. Fix the cause, not the symptom."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "kubernetes",
      "aside": "read the Events!",
      "subtitle": "Debug under pressure"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "kubectl Debug Cheatsheet",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Inspect first",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kubectl get pods -o wide # node, IP",
            "kubectl describe pod web # events",
            "kubectl get pod web -o yaml",
            "kubectl get events # timeline",
            "kubectl logs web # stdout"
          ],
          "note": "describe: events sit at the bottom"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Flag",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`-o wide`",
              "Adds node and IP"
            ],
            [
              "`-o yaml`",
              "Full live object"
            ],
            [
              "`-n ns`",
              "Pick a namespace"
            ],
            [
              "`-A`",
              "All namespaces"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Debug order",
          "text": "get, then describe, then logs --previous, then exec. Read Events before guessing."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Debug and roll out",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Goal",
            "Command"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Crashed run logs",
              "`logs web --previous`"
            ],
            [
              "Shell inside",
              "`exec -it web -- sh`"
            ],
            [
              "Ephemeral tools",
              "`debug -it web`"
            ],
            [
              "Local access",
              "`port-forward web 8080:80`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kubectl rollout status deploy/web",
            "kubectl rollout history deploy/web",
            "kubectl rollout undo deploy/web",
            "kubectl set image deploy/web c=v2",
            "kubectl scale deploy/web --replicas=5"
          ],
          "note": "undo returns to previous revision"
        },
